687
00:45:19,460 --> 00:45:23,160
And we came home that fall, and I called my grandma.

688
00:45:23,160 --> 00:45:24,480
I was so excited.

689
00:45:24,480 --> 00:45:27,440
I grew up Catholic, and I told her, I said, Grandma, I'm going to get baptized again.

690
00:45:27,440 --> 00:45:29,040
I just gave my life to the Lord.

691
00:45:29,040 --> 00:45:33,060
And she said, I'm sorry to hear you're leaving the church.

692
00:45:34,240 --> 00:45:37,620
And I, you know, sense of reconciled that, but I was kind of hurt.

693
00:45:37,620 --> 00:45:39,820
I was like, no, I get it.

694
00:45:39,820 --> 00:45:41,100
I finally get it.

695
00:45:41,100 --> 00:45:41,920
So we got baptized.

696
00:45:41,920 --> 00:45:43,220
My spiritual family was there.

697
00:45:43,220 --> 00:45:44,960
My Young Life leaders were there.

698
00:45:45,620 --> 00:45:56,400
But as I went through life and I volunteered, I'd see dads baptizing their children, you know, in the pools.

699
00:45:56,400 --> 00:45:59,740
And I would just leave and weep because I wanted that.

700
00:45:59,740 --> 00:46:05,400
So I started praying probably about 16 years ago before I knew I was having you, my wonderful daughter, Anna.

701
00:46:06,880 --> 00:46:13,600
And just praying, God, please, somehow, someway, let my life be a message to you.

702
00:46:13,600 --> 00:46:16,360
And I would just be praying this.

703
00:46:16,360 --> 00:46:18,140
So I'm very excited for today.

704
00:46:18,140 --> 00:46:21,200
Very excited for what has already happened in your heart.

705
00:46:21,200 --> 00:46:23,820
So I just encourage you guys.

706
00:46:23,820 --> 00:46:30,260
When I was in Young Life, I would meet with parents who, again, would weep over their kids and say, please, help, help.

707
00:46:30,260 --> 00:46:32,360
So this is a very big day.

708
00:46:32,360 --> 00:46:33,000
I'm very excited.

709
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:34,520
